Changes in this copy (dotfiles, 2026-10):
- SKILL.md: added a "Local rule (dotfiles)" bullet to the user contract
  requiring the report to state plainly that readers are AI-simulated.
- README.md: the Verify section referenced a test suite and eval files
  that are not vendored; rewrote it to point at the pinned explainer
  commit. Scoped the "runs offline / sends nothing" claim to the Python
  scripts (reader subagents still call the model).
- scripts/skim.py: word count now uses feed.nwords (CJK-aware ~2
  chars/word), first_sentence/first_words cut Japanese text at 。！？
  and without spaces, and the stats line labels the read-time estimate
  as a rough figure for CJK drafts (238 WPM is an English average).
- scripts/room.py: first_sentence_wrap also ends sentences at 。！？, and
  skips the first-sentence emphasis when the boundary falls inside an
  open inline tag (would split the tag across the span → crossing markup).
- scripts/signals.py: refuses drafts containing CJK text instead of
  returning English-metric counts that would read as valid data; SKILL.md
  step 5 documents the skip and moves the trust ledger to the step-6 read.
- SKILL.md "Adapting to your environment": file-mode fallback now writes
  sessions to `<run-dir>/<reader>/` so room.py / ask.py find them, and
  step 0's ~150-word gate uses feed.nwords' CJK convention.
- scripts/room_template.html: dropped the Google Fonts link/preconnect;
  the page renders with the existing local fallback stack and no longer
  makes external requests when opened.
